  ('ba84af46-07a2-5d48-917a-b497ef073d29', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-sentence-structure'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The marathon course winds through six neighborhoods, crosses two bridges, and finishes beside the harbor." Which statement about the sentence is accurate?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is a fragment because the subject appears only one time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"compound-predicate-misread"},{"text":"It is one complete sentence with a single subject and three verbs.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is a fused sentence because it needs a semicolon to be correct.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-overgeneralized"},{"text":"It is a comma splice because commas separate the three verbs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-misread-as-splice"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is one complete sentence with a single subject and three verbs.$q$, $q$The subject "course" has three verbs, "winds," "crosses," and "finishes," in a series, which is a compound predicate in one complete sentence. A comma splice requires two independent clauses, but here the commas separate verbs, not clauses.$q$, 'draft', null)
