   $q$Which choice contains a comma splice?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The satellite's battery was designed to last five years, it has now operated for eleven.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The satellite's battery, however, was designed to last only five years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"interrupter-misread-as-splice"},{"text":"Designed to last five years, the satellite's battery has now operated for eleven.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introductory-phrase-misread"},{"text":"The satellite's battery was designed to last five years, but it has now operated for eleven.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"compound-sentence-misread-as-run-on"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The satellite's battery was designed to last five years, it has now operated for eleven.$q$, $q$Two independent clauses, "battery was designed" and "it has now operated," are joined only by a comma. In the sentence with "however," the word interrupts a single clause, so the commas around it are correct.$q$, 'draft', null)
