   $q$Read the sentence: "The restoration crew faced one stubborn problem ___ original bricks no longer matched any clay available in the region." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"problem; because the","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-dependent-clause"},{"text":"problem, the","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"problem the","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"},{"text":"problem: the","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$problem: the$q$, $q$A colon can follow an independent clause to introduce an explanation, here the specific problem the crew faced. A comma alone between the two independent clauses would create a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
