   $q$Why does the writer include the information about the neighboring county in sentence 5?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To give background on how book wagons were first invented and paid for","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"To suggest that Fairweather once worked for the state-run wagon as well","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To show that a wagon that only delivered books, without taking requests, did not last","is_correct":true},{"text":"To show that the state government did not care about readers living on farms","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show that a wagon that only delivered books, without taking requests, did not last$q$, $q$The neighboring wagon also brought books to farms but used a fixed list, and it failed, which supports Baek's point that delivery alone was not enough. Nothing in the draft says the state did not care about readers; the contrast is about how titles were chosen.$q$, 'draft', 'd95e0f64-caa6-5efb-83c0-0c458f6a3d65')
