  ('486b952f-d852-56d1-a038-f23bdad0a445', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A classmate objects that the loans in sentence 7 may have grown only because more families moved to Larch County. Which detail from Baek's essay, if added, would best answer this objection?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Baek reports that the wagon added four new stops between 1905 and 1912.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-objection"},{"text":"Baek reports that farm families often shared borrowed books with neighbors who lived nearby.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"does-not-address-objection"},{"text":"Baek reports that Fairweather kept careful records of every book she lent.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Baek reports that the county's farm population stayed nearly the same between 1905 and 1912.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Baek reports that the county's farm population stayed nearly the same between 1905 and 1912.$q$, $q$If the population barely changed, a nearly sevenfold rise in loans cannot be explained by new families, so the objection loses its force. The four new stops actually feed the objection, because more stops could raise loans without any change in how Fairweather chose books.$q$, 'draft', 'd95e0f64-caa6-5efb-83c0-0c458f6a3d65')
