   $q$Which sentence should replace sentence 5 so that it states a claim the draft goes on to support?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mr. Abara is the most interesting character because he keeps his eyes closed while he works.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-analysis"},{"text":"Teodor and Mr. Abara both work as piano tuners in the same small town during one long winter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-claim"},{"text":"Pianos are difficult instruments to care for, and tuning them takes many years of practice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Okonjo-Hart contrasts the two tuners to set up Teodor's change from a hurried worker to a patient listener.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Okonjo-Hart contrasts the two tuners to set up Teodor's change from a hurried worker to a patient listener.$q$, $q$The rest of the draft traces how Teodor changes from rushing to listening, so a claim about that change fits the evidence. The summary choice only states who the characters are, not what the story shows.$q$, 'draft', 'ed20a3a4-dd83-52e9-ae1c-07011d2f86b0')
