   $q$A rectangular poster is $3$ centimeters longer than it is wide, and its area is $40$ square centimeters. What is its width?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$8.5$ centimeters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"treated-area-as-perimeter"},{"text":"$-8$ centimeters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"kept-negative-root"},{"text":"$5$ centimeters","is_correct":true},{"text":"$8$ centimeters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-in-factors"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$5$ centimeters$q$, $q$Let $w$ be the width. Then $w(w + 3) = 40$, so $w^2 + 3w - 40 = 0$, which factors as $(w + 8)(w - 5) = 0$. A width cannot be negative, so $w = 5$ centimeters, and the length is $8$ centimeters: $5 \cdot 8 = 40$. The value $8$ centimeters comes from writing the factors as $(w - 8)(w + 5)$, which multiplies to $w^2 - 3w - 40$.$q$, 'draft', null)
